{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"CLOSE BLOCKED - and correctly so. The AC-checkbox precheck surfaced that this story is NOT complete. 9 of 15 ACs are genuinely met and are now checked: the DETERMINISTIC check (all four fields, placeholder + enum semantics, advisory-and-never-blocking so pre-contract tickets are grandfathered), the overlay wiring (defined + activated, advisory, exec AGENT, [operator-attested] trigger), the rubric prompt existing + loadable + execution_mode: agentic, the declaration-syntax end-to-end pin, the shipped-contract-text digest guard, ADR-0061, and the no-world-measurement-reach guard.\n\nThe 6 REMAINING ACs all concern the AGENT criterion's RUNTIME BEHAVIOUR, and none of them is proven:\n (1) wrong-account escape catchable - rule (a) firing on 579718921998 declared vs 896586841071 in the Terraform backend;\n (2) CONTRAST at criterion level - a correctly-declared plan produces NO finding;\n (3) privilege_posture: broader flagged on a scoped-permission criterion, production-equivalent not - rule (c);\n (4) instrument checked independently of privilege_posture - rule (d), the escape-2b case;\n (5) NO-ANCHOR case produces no finding - rule (b);\n (6) the ADR-0054 corpus-replay false-positive rate that would justify promotion from advisory.\n\nWhat exists is the rubric TEXT stating all four rules; what does not exist is any eval fixture exercising them, so nothing demonstrates the criterion actually fires or stays silent as specified. The sibling project criteria each ship a .rebar/evals/<criterion>.eval.yaml; this one has none. That is the honest gap: the deterministic half and the wiring are done and tested, the behavioural half is asserted but unproven.\n\nNot force-closing. Change 1423 is LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 and can land on its own merit (the DET check and wiring are correct and independently useful), but this ticket should not be marked done until the eval fixtures exist and the FP rate is recorded."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785918715023392001,"uuid":"8e674615-054a-4886-806a-6a51d39fadb8"}